        "title": "So expensive I couldn't afford it.",
        "text": "I was looking forward to visiting the temple but when I arrived they told me it was 1000NR for foriegners (as usual with all tourist spots the locals or anyone that looks local gets in for free)\n\nWhilst I understand that they have to make money from tourists, most of the other sites in Kathmandu are only 250NR for entry. \n\nI genuinely could not afford to pay the admission fee, and I'm not sure if I did have the money would pay to go in.\n\nA man that worked at the ticket office followed me out and told me to come either very very early (6am) or late at night to get in for free as the ticket office would be shut. I'm not sure how much you would be able to see but it might be better than paying the hefty sum.\n\nI hate to leave a bad review but I would go and see all the other sites in Kathmandu and if you have money left, then visit the temple. \n\n",
