        "title": "Worth a visit at least once!",
        "text": "After having visited the temple a number of times in last few years, I can definitely say that the management has improved and the entire premise looked better maintained.\n\nThe shops selling Rudraksha and other temple offerings are away from the main Puja complex as they are on the path that leads to two entry gates of compound so one need not be worried about being bothered by sellers.\n\nA huge bull stands in front of the main temple inside the complex but clicking pictures within the premises is not allowed. I think I also read somewhere \"only Hindus allowed\" which is why I could see the other western tourists on the other side of river bank. \n\nThe river bank is not pleasing to eyes and mind from any sense as it is always dirty and to add up there are cremation processes that happen here.",
