      {
        "review_id": 247958195,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r247958195-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Beautiful temple, but poorly managed",
        "text": "For my fellow travelers, if you are visiting the temple for the first time\n\n1) Beware of Touts... Do not entertain them\n2) Do not purchase anything outside the temple, as it will not be taken for offering to the main deity (Pashupatinath)\n3) Poojas are performed in the temple. You need to book one day in advance at the poona counter\n4) Beware of Monkeys inside the temple, as they will snatch all the food that you carry\n5) Do not carry any cameras for Photography inside the temple\n6) Keep the foot wear outside the temple inside the bags hanged opposite to the foot wear resting place. Kindly give the bags inside the counter and collect a token\n7) Wash your feet and hands before entering the security cordon of the temple\n\nHope this helps all visitors",
