      {
        "review_id": 247701631,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r247701631-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Religious Place for the Hindus",
        "text": "The place is popular for its relevance in the Hindu Mythology and for its World Heritage Site status. If you know the story behind you may like the place. For all others it is a popular temple. The temple complex is comparatively clean compared to the extremely dirty Kathmandu city. Strange architecture is found. Lots of Pigeon capture a part of the complex. Whenever somebody walks there they all fly away together and again return after 1 minute. I enjoyed this view a lot. I think Pigeons are the best part of the temple. The entry to see the Pasupatinath's idol is restricted to the Hindus only and photography is not allowed. One needs to remove his/her shoes before getting inside.I was made to delete the two photos I took by the security personnel. The shrine is always overcrowded and in a stampede mode. No view of the peaks from this temple.",
