      {
        "review_id": 247571528,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r247571528-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Sacred Hindu Shrine",
        "text": "Its is one of the greatest hindu shrine of Lord Shiva, The entire area of Pashupatinath is a collection of ancient temples and also a UNESCO world heritage site. This place is also flooded with lot of monkeys be careful with them.They are a little more aggressive than any other place in Nepal. Also be careful of people sitting in the compound dressed up in saffron or yellow robes and with their foreheads painted with red and white ochre. These people might ask for 500 to 1000 NPR for a picture, don't get fooled by them. \nGoing back to the temple, its a beautiful piece of architecture with wooden sculptures and the nepalese 5 storied architecture. Ask for any wish you want he is the number one bestower of all wishes.\nThe only shock of my life was the public cremation on the banks of the river in the temple compound.",
